## 2. Test inspection: left vs right

Inspected `novacore/tests/test_outbox.py`: `test_events_are_chained_numbered_and_anchored`:
- Line 76: `self.assertEqual(_chain(fields, previous), event["chain_hash"])`
  - Left: `_chain(fields, previous)`, an independent reimplementation of the canonical JSON SHA-256 hash chaining formula defined in `test_outbox.py:26-29` according to the specification.
  - Right: `event["chain_hash"]`, generated by `CapabilityBroker.request()` invoking `chainlog.chain_hash()`.
- Line 79: `self.assertEqual({"count": 3, "head": previous}, anchor)`
  - Left: Literal expected dictionary `{"count": 3, "head": previous}`.
  - Right: `anchor`, parsed from `events.jsonl.anchor` written to disk by `chainlog.write_anchor()`.
The test verifies both the file content and the anchor metadata against independently computed values derived from the spec.

---

## 3. Deliberate break in the subject (sabotage test)

Target: `novacore/src/novacore/chainlog.py:64` in `check_tail()`.
Sabotage: Disabled the anchor equality check by replacing `if anchored != (count, head):` with `if False:`. This leaves the system vulnerable to tail truncation (accepting shorter valid chains when records are dropped from the end).

