## 6. Author limitations & honesty

Author reported:
- Clearly separated harness changes (oracle updates in 0e4519d and a75eaa1) from subject changes (6b93b6d and 134a45e), explaining the necessity of keeping directory context for anchor checks.
- Documented boundaries in `SCOPE.md` on what tail anchors can and cannot protect against (e.g. cannot protect against attackers with full write access to the directory, crash between append and anchor write fails closed).
- Explicitly documented that v1 logs are refused with no silent conversion.

